WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.102
-Let's talk about what
people are talking about,

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.570
what's going on in the news
right now.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:05.838
Over the weekend, it came out

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:07.440
that President Trump's
approval rating is at 36%.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.008
[ Audience groans ]

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:12.311
But Trump defended the number,
saying that it was "almost 40."

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:14.380
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.816
-Come on!
-He did.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.818
"Almost 40."

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.487
36%.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.722
Then he said,
"And if you read 36 upside down,

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.823
it looks like 93,
which is almost 100.

00:00:24.823 --> 00:00:26.359
So I'm doing amazing.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:30.929
Almost 100.
In Upside Down World."

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:33.466
But did you see that last week,
Trump's son Don Jr.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.236
tweeted screenshots of e-mails
from the Russian lawyer

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:39.438
who offered sensitive info
to his dad's campaign?

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:40.573
When he heard that his son

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.308
tweeted about
an ongoing investigation,

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.377
Trump was like, "The student
has become the master."

00:00:45.377 --> 00:00:47.213
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.415
-That's it.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:52.018
-"Wax on. Wax off."

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.220
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.023 --> 00:00:59.392
[ Laughs ]

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.527
In the meantime, the president
has hired a new lawyer.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:02.995
Did you see this guy?
-Yeah.

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:05.731
-[ Laughs ]
It's unbelievable.

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:09.168
He's hired a new lawyer.
His name is Ty Cobb.

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:10.403
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.938
It's his real name.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.873
Dude, Quest, I swear, man.
-Come on!

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.674
-His real name --
His name is Ty Cobb.

00:01:15.674 --> 00:01:17.377
To oversee
the White House response

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.678
to the Russia investigation.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.447
Show a picture. This is real.
That is the lawyer.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:24.350
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.653
Because nothing says
"My client's innocent"

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:29.122
like a lawyer who looks like
he's wearing a disguise.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.456
What is going --

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.358
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.861
"He's innocent!"

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.766
I don't know if he's
giving Trump legal advice

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.101
or talking to him
about "diabeetus."

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.103
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.038
[ Laughs ]

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:48.941
"Come over to this side
of the porch."

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:50.676
Trump just had his first trip
to France,

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:52.712
and at the end of his visit --
Did you see this?

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.481
He shook hands with
French President Emmanuel Macron

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.650
for a really long time.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.051
Did you see?
It's pretty strange.

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:01.087
We didn't do anything to this.
Watch this video.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.321
Here he goes.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:03.656
"How you doing?
Nice to see you.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.091
Pleasure to meet you.
Yeah. How you doing?

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.126
All right. Good. Yeah."
Tap, tap, tap.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:10.663
There you go. Pull.
A little yank, a little yank.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.298
Yeah, that's good.
And he's still holding.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.632
He's like -- This is real.

00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:16.769
And then
the French First Lady --

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.706
He gets her involved,
and they're grabbing.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.641
Now it's the circle of life.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.843
Now -- And then you again.
You get tapped.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:27.480
That's it. 30 seconds.
30-second handshake.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.516
That looked like a lame sitcom
where two characters

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:31.117
accidentally glue their hands
together.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:34.654
You know? It's like, "Ugh, ugh!
What are you going to do? Heh!"

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.222
[ Applause ]

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.056
You guys, last night
was the season premiere

00:02:38.056 --> 00:02:39.659
of "Game of Thrones."

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.026
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:43.663
No spoilers. No spoilers.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:47.600
But I saw that HBO's streaming
site crashed during the episode.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.968
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.536
That's how crazy
this show has gotten.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:51.837
They're killing off
websites now.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:52.805
-Really?

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:53.939
Everything --
-They don't care.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:55.108
-You don't know
who's going to survive.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.709
-Winter is here.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.945
-I saw that today
is World Emoji Day.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.079
Did you guys know that?
Yeah, of course.

00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:02.815
So in honor of that...

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.984
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.953
...we did some research
and found out

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.355
what was the inspiration
behind some popular emojis.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.790
-Really?
-Yeah, for example,

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.092 line:0%
this emoji was inspired
by Angela Merkel

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.294 line:0%
when she was listening
to Donald Trump.

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:18.331 line:0%
-Wow. Wow.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.266 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.668 line:0%
-This emoji was inspired

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.736 line:0%
by Ben Carson
at an important meeting.

00:03:24.736 --> 00:03:27.639 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:27.639 --> 00:03:30.776 line:0%
And finally, this emoji
was inspired by Donald Trump

00:03:30.776 --> 00:03:32.277 line:0%
when he's asked about Russia.

00:03:32.277 --> 00:03:34.247 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.852
More trouble
for United Airlines.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:40.987
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:42.922
The rapper ScHoolboy Q says

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:46.125
that they actually flew his dog
to the wrong city.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.293
Yeah. Then I guess
on the flight back,

00:03:48.293 --> 00:03:50.496
the dog had a fight over a seat
with Ann Coulter.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.831
-Really?!

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.766
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.868
-That's right.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.403
-Ah.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.472
-"This bitch gets my seat?"

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.374
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.276
It's a dog.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.545
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.380
It's a dog.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.116
Get this. On Friday,
a group of 40 turtles

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:13.652
caused delays on the runway
at JFK Airport.

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:15.755
On the bright side, the turtles
were moving so slow,

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.323
they got hired
to work at LaGuardia.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.658
"That's amazing.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.926
They're that slow.
They're that slow.

00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:22.995
It's amazing.
-Hey-yo!

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:25.731
-They're that slow!"

00:04:25.731 --> 00:04:27.700
This isn't good, guys.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.535
Millions of
Sabrett's hot dogs --

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.970
I love Sabrett's hot dogs.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.271
Millions of Sabrett's hot dogs

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.440
that are sold here on the street
in New York City

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.277
are being recalled because they
contain small pieces of bone.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:40.546
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.415
While the foreman
at the factory was like,

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.250
"Hey, has anyone seen Jeff?

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.387
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:50.990
When you see him,
tell him he's fired!"

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.492
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:56.028
"He hasn't been here
since the machine clogged up!"

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:58.330
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.000
"Oh, Jeff's wedding ring.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.002
He must have dropped it
in the hot-dog mixture!"

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.637
-"He's eloping
with a different lady!"

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:05.938
-"I'll go bring it to his house.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:08.674
I'll take the same shortcut home
that Jeff takes."

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:10.610
Whoa-ah!

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.978
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:14.914
[ Laughs ]

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.183
-"Where's Gary?!"

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:20.085
-"When you see Jerry,
tell him he's fired!

00:05:20.085 --> 00:05:22.654
Hey, Jerry's hat. He must
have dropped it in the hot dogs.

00:05:22.654 --> 00:05:25.758
I'll take the same shortcut
that Jerry takes!"

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:28.026
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.026 --> 00:05:30.029
[ Laughs ]

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:34.400
It's just -- Okay.
I don't know.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.268
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:38.504
Guys, millions of hot dogs
have been recalled

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:41.173
after small pieces of bone
were been found in them.

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:44.210
Street vendors are doing
their best to keep sales going.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.911
Just check out some of the new
signs that they've been using

00:05:45.911 --> 00:05:47.646
I saw today on the streets
of New York.

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:49.114
-You saw them?
-I walked around.

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:50.683
I brought my camera.
I took photos.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.185
-Of all the times?
-All the vendors.

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:53.786
-All over the city?
-Yeah.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:54.987
-Well, how nice of you.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.555
-I have one of those nice
Kodak Brownie cameras.

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:57.756
-Oh, my gosh!

00:05:57.756 --> 00:05:59.158
-Yeah.
It's a beautiful old camera.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:02.194
I got to get it developed.
-132-millimeter film.

00:06:02.194 --> 00:06:04.197
-[ Laughs ]
I walked around today,

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:05.665
and they're trying
to keep business going.

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:07.033
-God bless them.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.901
-So let's take a look
at some of the signs they have.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.770
This first one says, "Relax.
These hot dogs were made

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.938
years before
the bone problem started."

00:06:12.938 --> 00:06:14.339
Don't worry about it.
-Yeah.

00:06:14.339 --> 00:06:17.609
-Years ago.
-Yeah.

00:06:17.609 --> 00:06:20.613
-This next one says, "So what?
You got bones inside you, too."

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.847
-Yeah.

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:23.416
What's your problem?

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:24.917
[ Applause ]

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:26.418
I like this one.

00:06:26.418 --> 00:06:27.986
This one says,
"You want a boneless hot dog?

00:06:27.986 --> 00:06:30.590
What are you,
the queen of friggin' England?"

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.725
"What are you?"
-No!

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:35.127
"The queen of friggin' England."

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:36.895
Here's the last one here.

00:06:36.895 --> 00:06:38.297
It says,
"This cart is the original

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:40.633
famous bone-filled
hot dog cart."

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.735
That's the one to be at.
That's the one.

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:44.971
[ Applause ]

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.240
Oh, this really
made me laugh, guys.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.811
Last week, a man in Texas got
himself trapped inside an ATM.

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:55.213
Did you hear about this?
This is insane.

00:06:55.213 --> 00:06:57.049
This is a movie.
This is fantastic.

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:59.485
This is finally my one-man show.
I get to do this.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.621
Trapped in an ATM machine.

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:06.191
And he was slipping people notes
through the receipt slot

00:07:06.191 --> 00:07:08.560
that said "Help."

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.796
People taking money out
were like,

00:07:10.796 --> 00:07:12.064
"I knew my balance was low,
but what?

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:13.165
What do you mean, 'help'?

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:14.834
Oh, man. I'm in trouble, man."

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:17.670
[ Applause ]

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.639
That's right.
The guy got stuck in an ATM.

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:21.841
The man said that he was
excited to finally eat

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.642
then got himself trapped
in a vending machine.

00:07:23.642 --> 00:07:25.378
He's like, "Press B12!"

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:27.279
Guys, we have
a great show tonight.

00:07:27.279 --> 00:07:30.049
It's really fun!
The Roots right there!

